This repository bundles modified copies of two open-source projects.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
vectcut-api/
  Based on VectCutAPI by sun-guannan
  https://github.com/sun-guannan/VectCutAPI  (commit cfa4779a52f1dc59a56d90cc5868778eb50c6a97)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see vectcut-api/LICENSE).

  Changes made in this repository (each modified file carries a header notice):
  - web_preview.py, capcut_server.py: the Windows-only desktop_companion import
    is optional, so the server starts on macOS.
  - save_draft_impl.py: drafts are written straight into the local CapCut drafts
    folder (macOS and Windows), the folder is renamed to project_name, and
    draft_meta_info.json is rewritten (the template carried the original
    author's paths and ids).
  - add_effect_impl.py: effect parameters are passed in order (they were
    reversed, and an effect without parameters crashed).
  - add_audio_track.py, capcut_server.py: audio fade_in / fade_out.
  - add_image_impl.py, capcut_server.py: image rotation.
  - media_analysis.py (new): local Whisper transcription saved next to the video,
    pause detection, pause-free assembly with one shared media material, and
    subtitles generated from the transcript that follow the edit.
  - capcut_server.py: routes for the above; add_video records clip placement.
  - camera_moves.py (new): virtual camera moves from keyframes (sampled on every
    clip a move overlaps) and CapCut effects; /camera_moves and /add_camera_move.
  - save_draft_impl.py: media under ~/Movies is referenced in place (CapCut is
    sandboxed and can read that folder); a file used by many clips is copied once.
  - downloader.py: local files are cloned copy-on-write on macOS (APFS).
  - pyJianYingDraft/script_file.py: import_srt crashed when no font was given.
  - The upstream mcp-server/ folder (a copy of the project below) is not included.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
capcut-mcp-server/
  Based on capcut-mcp-server by Atx-Guy
  https://github.com/Atx-Guy/capcut-mcp-server  (commit d154070b94b1194894111f016d6dfeaf1a24966f)
  Licensed under the MIT License (see capcut-mcp-server/LICENSE).

  Changes made in this repository:
  - Responses: VectCutAPI returns its payload in "output", the tools read "result"
    (without this no tool worked).
  - Parameter names aligned with VectCutAPI: positions/scale, subtitles, keyframes
    (correct endpoint and format), stickers, effects, text background.
  - Real CapCut names for transitions, animations and effects instead of
    placeholder lists, plus a new capcut_list_types tool.
  - Local file paths accepted as media sources; target_start and track_name for
    timeline placement and layering; project_name on save; CapCut font-size scale.
  - The bundled backend is started automatically (services/backend.ts).
  - Content-aware tools (tools/media.ts): capcut_transcribe, capcut_detect_pauses,
    capcut_add_video_without_pauses (with alternating punch-in), capcut_add_auto_subtitles,
    capcut_add_camera_move.
